Create Agents for Microsoft 365 Copilot

Date: 2026-08-18
Platform / Environment: Microsoft Learn — Microsoft 365 / Copilot

What I Did

Completed a Microsoft Learn module covering AI-powered agents in Microsoft 365 Copilot, with a focus on agents that everyday business users can create without programming experience.

The module explored how these agents can be used within Microsoft SharePoint and Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat to assist with tasks, provide information, automate routine processes and improve productivity.

What I Learned

A key distinction covered in the module was between:

* Prebuilt agents — created by Microsoft or approved vendors and designed to provide functionality with minimal setup.
* User-created agents — agents that business users can create and manage without traditional programming skills.

These user-created agents can allow people across an organisation to apply AI to specific workflows without having to depend entirely on IT or software development teams.

Microsoft 365 Integration

I learned how agents can work alongside Microsoft 365 services such as:

* SharePoint
* Microsoft 365 Copilot Chat
* OneDrive
* Microsoft Teams

This can allow agents to work with organisational information and assist users within the tools they already use.

Security and Compliance

The module also covered the importance of security and compliance when introducing AI agents into an organisation.

Agents may interact with organisational information, so considerations such as protecting sensitive data, controlling access and ensuring appropriate compliance are important when deploying them.

Key Takeaways

The main takeaway for me was that AI agents are becoming more accessible to non-technical users.

The important part isn’t simply being able to create an agent. In a business environment, organisations also need to consider what information the agent can access, who can use it, and how that information is protected.

Practical Relevance

For IT support and Microsoft 365 administration, understanding agents is becoming increasingly relevant as organisations introduce AI into everyday workflows.

It also highlights an important shift in IT: supporting users may increasingly involve helping them use and govern AI tools, rather than only managing traditional applications and infrastructure.

Next Step

Continue building my understanding of Microsoft 365 Copilot and agents, with practical experience creating and configuring agents when an appropriate hands-on exercise becomes available.
